<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul sees pork imports, exports jumping this year.</title>
<headline>Seoul sees pork imports, exports jumping this year.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's pork imports are expected to surge 107 percent to 88,600 tonnes in 1997 compared with 42,800 tonnes a year ago, an official at the Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry said on Friday.</p>
<p>He said exports this year would gain 49 percent to 55,000 tonnes from 36,900 tonnes in 1996.</p>
</text>
